# What is Gitinit ?
- git init as creating an empty Git repository or reinitializing an existing one. It converts a normal directory into a Git repository.
It creates a normal directory into git repository using command Gitinit

 # Why do we need git init?

Suppose you have created a project manually:

DevOps-Project/
├── Dockerfile
├── app.py
└── requirements.txt

At this point, Git isn't managing the project.

You can start version control with:
cd DevOps-Project
git init

Now Git can track changes in that project.

The typical first-commit workflow is:

git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"

